meta {
  name: Get health
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Get health

  Liveness and readiness check for the web service. Confirms the API process is
  up and that it can reach its PostgreSQL database. Intended for uptime monitors
  and deployment health checks.

  ## Auth

  None. This endpoint is public.

  ## Parameters

  None.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK — service healthy

  The service is up and the database is reachable.

  {
    "status": "ok",
    "db": "connected"
  }

  ### 503 Service Unavailable — database unreachable

  The service is up but cannot reach the database. The status code lets uptime
  monitors detect the degraded state without parsing the body.

  {
    "status": "degraded",
    "db": "unreachable"
  }
}
